// ARTIFICIAL1. A Grand Prix at night in Port Artificial (a first-party world, published 18 Oct 2026 by migration 2026-10-18-artificial1).
//
// The lap is the 5,361.9 m Port Artificial street circuit, 17 turns, written as segments and never rescaled: the
// runtime builds it into a table every half metre (lib/runtime/gp-track.js) and races twenty cars on it, 3 laps, the
// five red lights, the Flap on three straights, track limits and places (lib/runtime/gp*.js). Every car is driven by an
// AI agent: yours is the WHY. V-07 (model-why-v07, given away by its owner under CC0; the WHY. wordmark stays the owner's
// mark), with Muse at the wheel for you ("MUSE · DRIVEN BY YOU"); the nineteen others are agents in ten invented teams,
// on the same car in their own colours. The world writes no player(), rival() or music (the cars and the sound are the
// runtime's).
//
// The look is two parts pasted above the world call: the scenery (S_: road, kerbs, barriers, city, harbour, stands, crowd, the pit
// building, the Black Box, the Spire, the baked night light) and the agents (A_: the twenty agents in their cars, the glass cockpit,
// the liveries). The podium and fireworks are not in yet (the runtime's stage slot is a stub).
/* ============================================================================================================
   SCENERY PART (gp merge, lane S). Section prefix S_. Paste it ABOVE the world's single world call.
   The round-3 night: road shader, kerbs, barriers, the baked light field, floodlight towers, sky and cloud deck,
   the city, harbour water, marina and yachts, stands and crowd, the pit building, the start gantry, the Black
   Box tunnel, the lighthouse and the Spire. It draws along the gp lap table (ctx.gp.table): the rig's centre line
   (every 5 m: x, y, z, width, bank, wall left, wall right) is refitted to the table at build, so the road, the
   kerbs and the barriers sit exactly where the cars drive.

   TOP-LEVEL NAMES (all S_): S_ASSETS, S_THEME, S_LOW, S_GRAPHICS, S_envExtras, S_fitLap, S_ST, S_build, S_update,
   S_make. Nothing else is declared at the top level (everything else lives inside S_make).

   THE WORLD CALLS (the world's own keys, beside the gp block):
     graphics: S_GRAPHICS,            // exposure, bloom, grade, environment extras, shadows { follow: 'hero' }, tier
                                      //   flags. Replaces the base world's graphics block (the old one is the
                                      //   moonlit M1 look: preset 'moonlit', environment x3)
     theme: S_THEME,
     assets: [ ...your own ids ].concat(S_ASSETS),   // 7 library ids: asphalt x3, concrete, stone wall, 2 athletes
     build(ctx) { S_build(ctx, ctx.gp); ... },       // ONCE. Needs ctx.gp.table (the lap table); also uses
                                      //   ctx.assets.texture / surface / human, ctx.instanced, ctx.water,
                                      //   ctx.textures.canvas, ctx.quality, ctx.camera, ctx.renderer, ctx.scene
     update(ctx, t, dt) { S_update(ctx, t, dt); ... },  // every frame: the light's direction at the car, the road's
                                      //   blur pre-filter, the glare, the crowd
   and the base world's own build() look code goes: no G.greybox() (the part draws the road, kerbs and barriers), no
   lamp posts, no ctx.sky, no ctx.water, no ctx.scene.fog and no lights (the part sets them: dome, FogExp2,
   a hemisphere light and the shadow light).

   WHAT IT NEEDS FROM THE REST:
     - the runtime's follow shadow light (graphics.shadows.follow 'hero', in S_GRAPHICS): the part adds the one
       castShadow DirectionalLight the runtime finds, and keeps only its direction (update); the runtime moves it
       onto the car (OW.hero).
     - corridor guard: every mesh sits under the group 'a1-scenery' (userData.gpFurniture), so the guard leaves the
       scenery alone (nothing is hidden, 0 warnings).
     - draws: 110 scenery meshes, 7 shadow casters, 1.40 M triangles; whole frame with 20 cars 231-266 calls on
       a laptop at 1600 x 900 (budget 300); the phone tier is the part's own (S_LOW: matches the runtime's 'low').
     - the agents part's lit wrapper: A_install(ctx, { lit: S_ST.lit }) after S_build: the scenery's lit-material
       function lit(material, k, { key, under }) (the baked light field on any material); S_ST also has carShade(cars),
       fieldAt(x, z) and lightDirAt(x, z, minEl, out).
     - debug record: window.__A1S (err[], ms_* build timings, fieldStats); S_ST.W is the same object.
   NOT IN THIS PART: the podium and the fireworks (the gp flow has a stage slot, GpStage.stage(env) in
   lib/runtime/gp-stage.js, but it is a stub and a world has no way to register a stage: see scratch-S notes), the
   rig's own cars, drivers, sparks, cameras and staging.
   ============================================================================================================ */
